{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and\nnothing else changes. `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'`\nrewrites the outline inputs that read it, recomputes the reference-set digests\nof the requirements it implements, rewrites `` `src/config.rs#fn[load]` `` in\ntheir rationales, and validation then passes without calling a model.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.reference_digest`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.rationale.addresses`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.equivalence`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.refactor.moved_function` describes a concrete case with stated outcomes: `fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and `habeas refactor --map ...` rewrites the outline inputs and recomputes the digests. It also rewrites the rationale address, and validation then passes without a model call. The test `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_function_keeps_its_evidence_current]` covers each outcome.\n\n- **Setup.** `project`, `config_source`, `author` and `write_evidence` build a fixture. `src/config.rs` carries `load`, `check` and `verify`. The fixture has two current records, `rules.load` and `rules.check`. Their reference digests come from `habeas::reference_set_digest_for`, and their outline inputs come from `habeas::outline_input`. The test asserts validation is clean before the move.\n- **Move.** `move_load(root, \"\")` moves `load` to `src/config/load.rs` byte-unchanged, with no other change. The test asserts validation then reports an error mentioning `fn[load]`, so the move really makes the evidence stale.\n- **Command.** It runs the real `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'` binary through `refactor` and asserts success. It asserts the report says `Changed 1 records:\\n- evidence/rules.load.json`.\n- **Outline inputs rewritten.** It asserts `record[\"inputs\"][1][\"file\"] == \"src/config/load.rs\"`.\n- **Digests recomputed and validation passes.** After the refactor it asserts `errors(root)` is empty, which means the `references` digest and all inputs are current again. `errors` calls `habeas::validate_repository` directly, so no model is involved.\n- **Rationale rewritten.** It asserts the exact new rationale. The span `` `src/config.rs#fn[load]` `` becomes `` `src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` ``. The plain mention `` `src/config.rs` `` for `verify` is left alone, and the report lists it for review.\n- **Nothing else changes.** `rules.check` is unchanged byte-for-byte and is absent from the report. A `snapshot` comparison of all other files, excluding `evidence/rules.load.json`, shows no other file changed.\n- **Idempotence.** A second run reports `Changed 0 records:`.\n\nThe cited requirements are covered for this case. The unchanged function lets the hash-match and digest-match conditions of `outline_inputs` and `reference_digest` hold, and the rewrite and the later passing validation show this. `rationale.addresses` is asserted through the rationale text. `equivalence` is asserted through the changed record passing validation afterwards. The negative cases, such as an edited function, belong to other tests and are not part of this example.",
